# Pi with a shell, POSIX tools and curl, and no compiler: the README's "Pi with npm",
# whose page installs five device host modules: display, input, download for
# the download tool of Pi's Dolly extension (Janis links its client), upload for
# its upload tool (the upload command), and html for its ask_user and show_html
# tools (the html command). The recipe engine lets an npm user build an image
# FROM it (dolly-build).
INSTALL /Dollyfile-core f92e986b840d0d46883b4a8d6eee8082aebd56f944f318083bda74cfe3e86b10
INSTALL /Dollyfile-dollyfile 05eb5138b6e5166673e5d445b74064d530ebd863aab9a937b5f32123d86f5cd5
INSTALL /Dollyfile-posix bd721815ffc3d3b9d887f57c3260749cb1db05ed2fe3f46a38b37e00ee66391b
INSTALL /Dollyfile-display a03812d93e51c6338e43063f954fb9492ee0535f94a39e5c377d504a3d9eedb8
INSTALL /Dollyfile-curl bce8c6fafa9e15aa65c9804fc4fec07a309e6174c8e1cb80b7396ac6e458431e
